# ─── Ignore all, then opt in what makes the repo shareable ───
# Bonus: build output and dependencies (node_modules, .svelte-kit, …) stay out
# for free. Nothing is tracked until it is listed below.
#
# NOTE: git has no inline comments. A '#' starts a comment only at the start of
# a line. Keep each rule on its own line.
*

# Let git go into subdirectories (nested files stay ignored until listed)
!*/

# Hard-ignore generated, dependency and editor directories. These come after
# `!*/` so that they win. The opt-ins below cannot bring back their contents.
node_modules/
.svelte-kit/
.wrangler/
build/
dist/
.claude/
.vscode/

# ─── Opt back in: source and config ───
!.gitignore
!.npmrc
!.node-version
!.tool-versions
!.env.example
!README.md
!LICENSE
!package.json
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!*.yml
!*.yaml
!*.jsonc
!*.json
!tsconfig*.json
!*.config.js
!*.config.ts
!*.svelte
!*.ts
!*.js
!*.mjs
!*.css
!*.svg
!*.html
!*.md
!*.txt

# ─── Dev-only: re-ignore AFTER the opt-ins, so that these win ───
# The underscore convention (_PLAN.md, _NOTES.md, …)
_*
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# ─── Secrets ───
# The opt-ins above are by EXTENSION, and an extension cannot tell a config file
# from a secret: `credentials.json` matched `!*.json` and was trackable. These
# rules come after them, so a file named like a secret is ignored whatever its
# extension.
#
# KNOW THE LIMIT. These match a NAME, and a name can be anything. They are also
# case-sensitive on Linux: `service-account.json` is caught and
# `serviceAccount.json` is not. Enumerating every spelling is a game nobody
# wins. This is a safety net under care, and not a substitute for it. Run
# `git status` before you commit, and keep a real secret out of the tree.
*secret*
*credential*
*token*
*password*
*apikey*
*api-key*
*service-account*
*serviceaccount*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.env*
!.env.example

# Generated by `wrangler types`. It is a build product of wrangler.jsonc.
worker-configuration.d.ts
